<section xml:id="_method_1_powershell_command_line_quick_install_recommended">
<title>Method 1: PowerShell Command-Line Quick Install (Recommended)</title>
<simpara>Install and configure Mello-Workspace directly from PowerShell without manual cloning. This downloads the latest archive, provisions AutoHotkey v2 binaries into <literal>ahkbin/</literal>, configures the Start Menu shortcut, and starts the workspace.</simpara>
<programlisting language="powershell" linenumbering="unnumbered"># Launch PowerShell and run the remote installation one-liner:
irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/voltaire-toledo/Mello-Workspace/main/Mello-Workspace.ps1 | iex <co xml:id="CO1-1"/></programlisting>
<calloutlist>
<callout arearefs="CO1-1">
<para>Automatically invokes <literal>Install-FromUrl</literal>, backs up any previous installation to <literal>%LOCALAPPDATA%\Mello-Workspace\backup-*</literal>, downloads dependencies, and registers the application.</para>
</callout>
</calloutlist>
<note>
<simpara>The installer stores application files in <literal>%LOCALAPPDATA%\Mello-Workspace</literal> and registers a clean shortcut under <literal>Start Menu &gt; Programs &gt; Mello</literal>.</simpara>
</note>
</section>
<section xml:id="_method_2_git_clone_local_script_execution">
<title>Method 2: Git Clone &amp; Local Script Execution</title>
<simpara>For users who prefer managing the repository via Git:</simpara>
<programlisting language="powershell" linenumbering="unnumbered"># 1. Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/voltaire-toledo/Mello-Workspace.git
cd Mello-Workspace

# 2. Run the deployment script locally <co xml:id="CO2-1"/>
.\Mello-Workspace.ps1

# 3. (Alternative) Launch directly with AutoHotkey v2 <co xml:id="CO2-2"/>
.\ahkbin\AutoHotkey32.exe .\Mello-Workspace.ahk</programlisting>
<calloutlist>
<callout arearefs="CO2-1">
<para>When executed locally, <literal>Mello-Workspace.ps1</literal> detects the repository workspace, fetches required runtime binaries into <literal>ahkbin/</literal> if missing, sets up Start Menu shortcuts, and starts MWS.</para>
</callout>
<callout arearefs="CO2-2">
<para>Direct invocation when development binaries are already in place.</para>
</callout>
</calloutlist>
</section>
<section xml:id="_method_3_developer_setup_via_taskfile">
<title>Method 3: Developer Setup via Taskfile</title>
<simpara>If you are contributing or customizing features, initialize your local environment using the included developer script or <literal>task</literal>:</simpara>
<programlisting language="powershell" linenumbering="unnumbered"># Run developer provisioning and git pre-commit hook setup
.\scripts\setup-dev.ps1

# Or run using Task
task setup</programlisting>
<simpara><?asciidoc-hr?></simpara>
</section>
</section>
